There is no conventional frontperson. Nalin determines phrase shape and decay; Ellis decides which pieces of the break are allowed to survive around it; Ploy extends selected figures into a different register; Arun converts drum vacancies into hand-played punctuation; Lena adds low reed weight without turning the arrangement into a continuous bass layer. Live versions vary because plectrum angle, fret pressure, string age, room reflection, and the exact length of every acoustic decay change how much space the drum edits require.

